input.script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'zshrc-review',
  description: 'Multi-dimension review of .zshrc with adversarial verification',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Review', detail: 'four parallel reviewers: perf, correctness, security, structure' },
    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'adversarial verification of each finding' },
  ],
}

const FILE = '/Users/naokisega/src/github.com/nsega/dotfiles/.zshrc'

const FINDINGS_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    findings: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          title: { type: 'string' },
          lines: { type: 'string', description: 'line number(s) in .zshrc, e.g. "91-92, 99"' },
          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['high', 'medium', 'low'] },
          description: { type: 'string', description: 'what is wrong and why it matters' },
          suggestion: { type: 'string', description: 'concrete fix' },
        },
        required: ['title', 'lines', 'severity', 'description', 'suggestion'],
      },
    },
  },
  required: ['findings'],
}

const VERDICT_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    isReal: { type: 'boolean' },
    note: { type: 'string', description: 'evidence for the verdict; if refuted, why' },
    revisedSuggestion: { type: 'string', description: 'improved fix if the original suggestion was wrong or suboptimal; empty string if original stands' },
  },
  required: ['isReal', 'note', 'revisedSuggestion'],
}

const COMMON = `You are reviewing a zsh configuration file at ${FILE} on macOS (Apple Silicon, Homebrew at /opt/homebrew). Read the file first. The user is a DevOps/cloud engineer using Oh My Zsh, Ghostty terminal, and the herdr multiplexer. You may run read-only shell commands (zsh -n, command -v, ls, etc.) to check facts on this machine, but do NOT modify any files or shell state. Report only genuine issues found in THIS file; no generic advice. Each finding needs exact line numbers.`

const DIMENSIONS = [
  {
    key: 'perf',
    prompt: `${COMMON}

Dimension: SHELL STARTUP PERFORMANCE. Find everything that slows down interactive shell startup: repeated or redundant initialization (e.g. compinit called multiple times, version-manager init run twice), expensive subshells/evals/source-from-process-substitution executed on every startup (kubectl/stern/pixi completion generation, brew --prefix calls), completions that could be cached to a static file or lazy-loaded via fpath, redundant PATH manipulation. For each, explain the mechanism and estimate relative cost (which ones dominate). Suggest concrete fixes (caching, fpath-based completion, single guarded compinit, lazy init).`,
  },
  {
    key: 'correctness',
    prompt: `${COMMON}

Dimension: CORRECTNESS BUGS. Find actual bugs and broken/dead configuration: PATH entries that point at files instead of directories or that duplicate each other, init code run twice with different behavior, variables set under misleading comments, copy-pasted duplicate blocks, quoting bugs in functions (word splitting on paths with spaces), logic errors in conditionals (e.g. substring matching used for path prefix checks), stale references to tools that may not exist, macOS vs GNU command incompatibilities (e.g. stat -c) including any hidden ordering dependencies that currently mask them. Verify claims by inspecting the file and, where useful, checking this machine (command -v, ls). Exact line numbers required.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'security',
    prompt: `${COMMON}

Dimension: SECURITY. Review for security-relevant weaknesses: ZSH_DISABLE_COMPFIX disabling completion-directory safety checks, sourcing generated files or process substitutions from tools on PATH at startup, the 1Password cache handling (file perms, TTL check, failure paths, whether the cache could be read or poisoned), history settings leaking secrets, any world-writable or predictable paths. Only report issues that are real for a single-user macOS machine; skip theoretical multi-user concerns unless the code makes them trivially exploitable. Exact line numbers required.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'structure',
    prompt: `${COMMON}

Dimension: STRUCTURE AND MAINTAINABILITY. Review organization: leftover Oh My Zsh template boilerplate comments, settings scattered or duplicated across the file (PATH exports in five places, two openjdk versions on PATH, completions initialized in four places), sections whose comments do not match their content, the tail of the file accumulating tool-appended blocks (Docker Desktop twice), opportunities to restructure into clearly ordered sections (env/PATH -> plugins -> omz -> completions -> aliases -> functions -> secrets) or split into sourced fragments, dead or commented-out template noise worth deleting. Also check whether the repo CLAUDE.md description (rbenv/pyenv/nodenv) still matches reality (volta, bun present). Prioritize changes by payoff; do not suggest a rewrite for its own sake. Exact line numbers required.`,
  },
]

phase('Review')
log('Fanning out 4 reviewers: perf, correctness, security, structure')

const results = await pipeline(
  DIMENSIONS,
  d => agent(d.prompt, { label: `review:${d.key}`, phase: 'Review', schema: FINDINGS_SCHEMA }),
  (review, d) => {
    if (!review || !review.findings.length) return []
    log(`review:${d.key} -> ${review.findings.length} findings, verifying`)
    return parallel(review.findings.map(f => () =>
      agent(
        `${COMMON}

You are an adversarial verifier. A reviewer claims the following issue in ${FILE}:

TITLE: ${f.title}
LINES: ${f.lines}
SEVERITY: ${f.severity}
CLAIM: ${f.description}
PROPOSED FIX: ${f.suggestion}

Try to REFUTE this. Read the exact lines in context. Check facts on this machine with read-only commands where relevant (e.g. does the flag/behavior actually exist in zsh, does the tool exist, does execution order mask the issue, is the claimed cost real). If the issue is real but the proposed fix is wrong, incomplete, or would break something else in this file, say so and give a corrected fix in revisedSuggestion. Set isReal=false if the claim is wrong, purely stylistic with no benefit, or does not apply to this setup.`,
        { label: `verify:${d.key}:${f.title.slice(0, 40)}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICT_SCHEMA }
      ).then(v => ({ dimension: d.key, ...f, verdict: v }))
    ))
  }
)

const all = results.filter(Boolean).flat().filter(Boolean)
const confirmed = all.filter(f => f.verdict && f.verdict.isReal)
const refuted = all.filter(f => f.verdict && !f.verdict.isReal)
log(`${confirmed.length} confirmed, ${refuted.length} refuted`)
return { confirmed, refuted: refuted.map(f => ({ title: f.title, why: f.verdict.note })) }

